# L §5.14.3 (round 12): flows' "unit is that of the places it reads (x's, or the leg's places' for a move), known at
# load where they have one fixed unit": over a span with no movement, the flows of konto (unit PLN) and of wage (its
# leg's amount is money PLN) are 0.00 PLN. (Writer 5's T-70..T-72, the empty-span half.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

move wage[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  dom = 10
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask q1: flows(konto, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-01-05)
ask q2: flows(wage, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-01-05)
=== expect
q1: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
